---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Colophon" description="How teofurlan.com is built, and the tooling credits.">
  <h1>Colophon</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Stack</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Astro 7, built to static pages and served from Cloudflare Workers static assets.</li>
      <li>Type: IBM Plex Sans and IBM Plex Mono, self-hosted.</li>
      <li>Images are resized and stripped of metadata at build time with Sharp.</li>
      <li>Two themes, dark blueprint and light paper. They follow your system setting until you pick one.</li>
      <li>Works without JavaScript. Scripts only add the theme toggle, the drafting-grid pointer, the scroll drawings and the email link.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Tooling</h2>
    <p>
      Built with the <a href="https://github.com/Gentleman-Programming/gentle-ai">gentle-ai</a> harness and
      <a href="https://www.aihero.dev">AI Hero</a> skills. The whole build conversation with the coding agent is on
      <a href="/build-session/">How this site was built</a>.
    </p>
    <p>Copy edited with an LLM. The raw build conversation is on that page, in Spanish.</p>

    <h2>Daily decoration</h2>
    <p>The small drawing on the home page is static for now. A daily generated piece, with the model and prompt shown next to it, comes later; its archive will live at <a href="/decoration/">/decoration/</a>.</p>

    <h2>Feeds</h2>
    <p><a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed for the writing section</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
